<script type="application/json" id="sc-catalog">{{ scriptCheckPayload | safe }}</script>
<main class="sc-page">
  <div class="sc-hero-shell">
    <nav class="sc-wrap sc-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Cold call script checker</span></nav>
    <section class="sc-wrap sc-hero" aria-labelledby="sc-title">
      <div><p class="sc-eyebrow">Free B2B sales resource / Built for a better conversation</p><h1 id="sc-title">Check your<br>cold call <span>opening.</span></h1><p class="sc-lead">Paste your draft. Check the wording, explore relevant examples and build an opening you can practise.</p><div class="sc-actions"><a class="sc-button" href="#sc-builder">Check my opening <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="sc-text-link" href="#sc-example">See a worked example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="sc-hero-note">Free. No email required. Your draft stays on this page.</p></div>
      <aside class="sc-hero-sheet" aria-label="A practical change to a sales opening"><div class="sc-sheet-top"><span>GIVE THEM A REASON TO TALK</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><p class="sc-sheet-before">“We help businesses<br>improve efficiency.”</p><span class="sc-sheet-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><p class="sc-sheet-after">“How does your team check which subscriptions are still being used?”</p><p class="sc-sheet-foot">Illustrative SaaS example.<br>A specific question gives the buyer somewhere to start.</p></aside>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="sc-builder-section" id="sc-builder" aria-labelledby="sc-builder-title"><div class="sc-wrap">
    <div class="sc-section-heading"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">01 / Bring your draft</p><h2 id="sc-builder-title">Who are you calling?<br>What do you say?</h2></div><p>A role, a short explanation of your offer and your current opening. That is enough to get started.</p></div>
    <noscript><p class="sc-notice">Enable JavaScript to use the checker. The worked example and review criteria below are available without it.</p></noscript>
    <div class="sc-workspace">
      <div id="sc-tool" class="sc-input-panel" role="group" aria-label="Cold call opening inputs" data-clarity-mask="true">
        <div class="sc-field"><label for="sc-buyer">Who are you calling?</label><input id="sc-buyer" type="text" list="sc-buyer-options" maxlength="100" required autocomplete="off" placeholder="For example, CFO at a SaaS company" aria-describedby="sc-buyer-help"><datalist id="sc-buyer-options">{% for buyer in scriptCheckPage.buyers %}<option value="{{ buyer }}"></option>{% endfor %}</datalist><p id="sc-buyer-help">Choose a suggested role or type your own. Add the industry if it helps.</p></div>
        <div class="sc-field"><label for="sc-offer">What do you sell, and who does it help?</label><textarea id="sc-offer" maxlength="500" rows="3" required placeholder="We help finance teams find unused software subscriptions before they renew." aria-describedby="sc-offer-help"></textarea><p id="sc-offer-help">One or two sentences. Include the practical problem your offer helps solve.</p></div>
        <div class="sc-field"><div class="sc-label-row"><label for="sc-script">Paste your opening</label><span id="sc-script-count">0 / 4,000</span></div><textarea id="sc-script" maxlength="4000" rows="7" required placeholder="Hi, this is…" aria-describedby="sc-script-help sc-script-count"></textarea><p id="sc-script-help">Include your first question and meeting request if you have them. Remove confidential details and personal contact information.</p></div>
        <div class="sc-actions"><button id="sc-check" class="sc-button" type="button" disabled>Check my opening <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button id="sc-clear" class="sc-text-button" type="button">Clear entries</button></div>
        <p id="sc-error" class="sc-notice" role="alert" hidden></p><p id="sc-status" class="sc-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
        <p class="sc-privacy-note">Checks run in your browser. This tool does not send your entries or edited draft to CallTeam. <a href="#sc-privacy">Read how your text is handled.</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="sc-builder-aside"><p class="sc-eyebrow">A useful starting point</p><h3>Check the wording.<br>Build your next draft.</h3><ol><li><strong>See what the text contains.</strong><span>Get specific observations with the wording behind them.</span></li><li><strong>Decide what needs work.</strong><span>Review possible issues and confirm what fits your buyer.</span></li><li><strong>Choose your starting point.</strong><span>Keep your opening, adapt a relevant example or use a general structure.</span></li><li><strong>Make it yours.</strong><span>Edit the draft, then copy or download it to practise.</span></li></ol><div class="sc-sample-picker"><p>Try a sample draft</p>{% for example in scriptCheckPage.examples %}<button type="button" class="sc-sample-button" data-sc-example="{{ example.id }}">{{ example.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>{% endfor %}<small>Fictional inputs. Every sample runs through the same checks as your own draft.</small></div></aside>
    </div>
    <section id="sc-results" class="sc-results" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="sc-results-title" data-clarity-mask="true" hidden>
      <div class="sc-result-heading"><div><p id="sc-result-mode" class="sc-eyebrow">Your wording / Your review</p><h2 id="sc-results-title">Here’s what your draft shows.</h2></div></div><p id="sc-summary" class="sc-result-summary"></p><div id="sc-metrics" class="sc-metrics" aria-label="Draft measurements"></div>
      <div class="sc-review-columns"><div id="sc-found-block"><h3>What the checker found</h3><ul id="sc-found" class="sc-findings"></ul></div><div id="sc-review-block"><h3>Worth reviewing</h3><ul id="sc-review" class="sc-findings"></ul></div><div id="sc-confirm-block"><h3>For you to confirm</h3><ul id="sc-confirm" class="sc-findings"></ul></div></div>
      <div class="sc-matched-heading"><p class="sc-eyebrow">Published examples / Your choice</p><h3>Resources to consider</h3><p>These are possible matches to words in your buyer and offer. Read why they appeared, then decide whether the approach fits.</p></div><div id="sc-resources" class="sc-resources"></div>
      <div class="sc-draft-choices"><h3>Choose how to build your draft.</h3><p>Use an example only if it fits your offer. You can also keep your own words or start with a general structure.</p><div id="sc-template-options" class="sc-template-options" role="group" aria-label="Choose a published script example"></div><div class="sc-actions"><button id="sc-keep" class="sc-button sc-button-secondary" type="button">Keep my opening <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button id="sc-general" class="sc-text-button" type="button">Use a general structure <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div></div>
      <div id="sc-draft-panel" class="sc-draft-editor" data-clarity-mask="true" hidden><div class="sc-editor-heading"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">Your editable draft</p><h3>Make every line yours.</h3></div><p id="sc-draft-source"></p></div><ul id="sc-draft-notes" class="sc-draft-notes"></ul><div class="sc-field"><label for="sc-draft-opening">Your opening</label><textarea id="sc-draft-opening" rows="6" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="sc-draft-help"></textarea></div><div class="sc-draft-pair"><div class="sc-field"><label for="sc-draft-followup">Your follow-up question</label><textarea id="sc-draft-followup" rows="4" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="sc-draft-help"></textarea></div><div class="sc-field"><label for="sc-draft-meeting">Your meeting request</label><textarea id="sc-draft-meeting" rows="4" maxlength="8000" aria-describedby="sc-draft-help"></textarea></div></div><p id="sc-draft-help" class="sc-draft-help">Replace placeholders, check your claims and adjust the wording to the buyer’s answers. A meeting request should follow a relevant conversation.</p><p id="sc-draft-status" class="sc-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p></div>
      <div class="sc-save-actions"><button id="sc-copy" class="sc-button sc-button-secondary" type="button">Copy review and draft <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button id="sc-download" class="sc-text-button" type="button">Download .txt <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button><p id="sc-copy-status" class="sc-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
      <p class="sc-result-limit">A wording check cannot establish buyer fit or predict booking rates. Review the suggestions, practise the draft and use real conversations to decide what works.</p>
      <div class="sc-result-cta"><div><h3>Ready to put this draft to work?</h3><p>Talk through the audience, offer and next step with CallTeam.</p></div><a class="sc-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sc-booking>Talk Through My Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sc-example-section" id="sc-example" aria-labelledby="sc-example-title"><div class="sc-wrap">
    <div class="sc-section-heading"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">02 / A CallTeam editorial example</p><h2 id="sc-example-title">From a broad pitch<br>to a useful question.</h2></div><p>Our editorial example shows one way to improve a fictional SaaS opening. This before-and-after explanation is separate from the tool’s automatic checks.</p></div>
    <div class="sc-example-comparison"><article><p class="sc-eyebrow">The original opening</p><blockquote>{{ scriptCheckPage.examples[0].input.script }}</blockquote><p>The caller moves from broad claims straight to a demo. The buyer has little opportunity to explain whether the offer is relevant.</p></article><article><p class="sc-eyebrow">An edited version</p><blockquote>{{ scriptCheckPage.editorialExample.opening }}</blockquote><p>The offer is specific. The question is connected to the CFO’s work. The caller can now listen before choosing the next step.</p></article></div>
    <div class="sc-example-note"><p><strong>What changed?</strong> The introduction stays. Unsupported superlatives come out. A practical question replaces the immediate demo request.</p><button type="button" class="sc-text-button" data-sc-example="saas">Check the original draft <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
  </div></section>

  <section id="sc-method" aria-labelledby="sc-method-title"><div class="sc-wrap sc-method-grid"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">03 / What the review looks for</p><h2 id="sc-method-title">How your opening is reviewed.</h2><p>Fixed rules check specific patterns in your text. Your buyer and offer help surface resources to consider. The findings show what was detected, what may need attention and what you need to judge yourself.</p><p>CallTeam’s <a href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/">{{ callScripts.length }} free B2B scripts</a> provide examples by buyer, industry and conversation objective. The <a href="/articles/cold-call-coaching-scorecard/">coaching scorecard</a> goes further when you are reviewing actual calls.</p></div><ol class="sc-criteria">{% for item in scriptCheckPage.criteria %}<li><span aria-hidden="true">0{{ loop.index }}</span><div><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.text }}</p></div></li>{% endfor %}</ol></div></section>

  <section class="sc-proof-section" aria-labelledby="sc-proof-title"><div class="sc-wrap sc-proof-grid"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">04 / Real campaign work</p><h2 id="sc-proof-title">Make the message<br>fit the market.</h2><p>In CallTeam’s published manufacturing cybersecurity campaign, the approach connected security services to production uptime, connected systems and recovery readiness.</p><p>The case study explains the targeting, conversations, qualification and follow-up behind the campaign. Those decisions provide useful context for a script.</p><a class="sc-text-link" href="/case-studies/manufacturing-cybersecurity-appointment-setting/">Read the manufacturing cybersecurity case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><aside class="sc-proof-note"><span>THE PRACTICAL LESSON</span><p>Start with the buyer’s operating problem.<br>Then connect the service.</p><small>This past campaign is separate from the fictional examples above. It does not measure or validate the checker’s results.</small></aside></div></section>

  <section class="sc-faq-section" aria-labelledby="sc-faq-title"><div class="sc-wrap sc-faq-grid"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">05 / Before you use it</p><h2 id="sc-faq-title">A few useful<br>answers.</h2><p>For a deeper look at building the whole conversation, read our <a href="/articles/how-to-write-a-b2b-cold-call-script/">B2B cold call script-writing guide</a>.</p></div><div class="sc-faqs">{% for faq in scriptCheckPage.faqs %}<details{% if loop.index == 7 %} id="sc-privacy"{% endif %}><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

  <section class="sc-next-section" aria-labelledby="sc-next-title"><div class="sc-wrap sc-next-grid"><div><p class="sc-eyebrow">06 / Turn the draft into a campaign</p><h2 id="sc-next-title">Let’s build your<br>outbound campaign.</h2><p>Bring your offer and the people you need to reach. We’ll talk through the targeting, calling, qualification and follow-up needed to turn the approach into real conversations.</p><div class="sc-actions"><a class="sc-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sc-booking>Talk Through My Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside><span class="sc-eyebrow">Still exploring?</span><a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/" class="sc-next-link"><strong>See how we’d run your campaign.</strong><p>Choose your market and buyer to explore a starting approach.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/services/sdr-training/" class="sc-text-link">Explore SDR training <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></aside></div></section>
</main>
